# P1 implementation report

## Status

P1 implementation is complete and source-frozen at `core/pit_optimizer_v5/campaign_admission.py`, SHA-256 `7e15ed500121b4c85df7a838feab51750e1f476a3e5427b9d1a0b1f0f58a89d9`.

## Implemented

- Added the exact frozen/slotted `CampaignAdmissionPolicyV5`, `CampaignAdmissionBindingV5`, and `AuthenticatedCampaignAdmissionV5` shapes without changing any existing serialized type.
- Added prepared-policy authentication for the exact paid development manifest graph, policy/config digests, provider config type, repository root identity, single-candidate search, zero retries/repairs, target/call/token capacity, and conservative finite-USD capacity.
- Added immutable selected-enrollment discovery across the union of value and authority namespaces. It enforces canonical manifest keys, detects foreign-key bindings, rejects missing/corrupt halves, honors an exact expected policy pin, and makes its sole typed-state read with `repair=False`.
- Added the pure exact role-envelope check using `prospective_role_usage_v5`. It also requires the request's fixed output cap to match the provider authority.
- Added the pure campaign-boundary decision with target-first completion and conservative missing-round attempt/call/token/USD reserve checks. Actual over-cap counters are treated as insufficient reserve rather than rejected as impossible history.
- Finite-USD arithmetic applies the greater authenticated unit price to the maximum input/output split, preserves the provider's explicit 50-digit `ROUND_CEILING` operation chain, computes required call products under the same conservative context, and compares the cap to `sum_cost_usd_v5` rather than subtracting under ambient Decimal context.

